<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan approves US$80.8 mln in China investments.</title>
<headline>Taiwan approves US$80.8 mln in China investments.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's economics ministry said on Tuesday it had approved 17 proposals for investment in rival China worth US$80.749 million.</p>
<p>The ministry agreed to let President Enterprises, Taiwan's biggest investor in the mainland, pour an additional US$12 million in a hypermarket project in Chongqing in southwestern Sichuan province.</p>
<p>President already had invested US$900 million in various projects in China.</p>
</text>
